# id damage delay spread clip numclips reloaddelay walkingspeed bulletspeed viewangle cost type firemode pellets scope category teams [muzzleflash impact...] [projectiletype] name
# 0.0 viewangle disables scope
# HOW TO ADD A WEAPON
# The first line is the number (count) of weapon records loaded. +1 everytime when you add a new weapon.
# When adding ID 64 (maximum) for example, the count should be 65 (maximum 128).
# Insert every new weapon record ABOVE these notes. Do not put blank.
# Do not put comment lines between records included by the count.
# Keep IDs sequential and equal to the record position: 0, 1, 2, ... 127.
# The ID selects the matching 32x32 cell in guns.PNG and gunsground.png.
# With the 128-pixel-wide sheets, each row contains four IDs.
#
# RECORD FORMAT (legacy 18/19 values, or the full 29-field rocket format)
# id damage delay spread clip numclips reloaddelay walkingspeed bulletspeed viewangle cost type firemode pellets scope category teams [muzzleflash] name
#
# id             Weapon ID, matching its record position and sprite cell.
# damage         Base damage per bullet (actual bullet damage varies slightly).
# delay          Time between shots in milliseconds; lower is faster.
# spread         Weapon spread/recoil angle in radians; lower is more accurate.
# clip           Rounds loaded in one magazine.
# numclips       Total magazines supplied, including the initially loaded one.
# reloaddelay    Reload duration in milliseconds.
# walkingspeed   Movement-speed multiplier while this weapon is equipped.
# bulletspeed    Projectile-speed multiplier; normal firearms usually use 1.0.
# viewangle      View-cone half-angle in radians; 0.0 disables the cone effect.
# cost           Buy-menu price.
# type           Inventory slot: 0=PRIMARY, 1=SECONDARY, 2=KNIFE, 3=GRENADE.
# firemode       Trigger mode: 0=SEMI (one shot per press), 1=AUTO (hold to fire).
# pellets        Projectiles per shot: 1=normal; values such as 4 or 6=shotgun.
# scope          Camera scope: 0=NONE, 1=LOW, 2=MEDIUM, 3=HIGH.
# category       Buy menu: 0=HIDDEN, 1=PISTOLS, 2=SHOTGUNS, 3=SMG,
#                4=RIFLES, 5=MACHINEGUNS, 6=EQUIPMENT.
# teams          Buy availability: 0=NONE, 1=T only, 2=CT only, 3=BOTH.
# muzzleflash    Optional flash ID before name, from 0 through 127.
#                0=muzzleflash.png; N uses the resources.txt key
#                muzzle_flash_N. Missing resource keys safely use style 0.
#                Omit this field to use 0 with old 18-value weapon rows.
# projectiletype Optional field before name when all impact fields are present:
#                0=normal bullet, 1=impact-detonated rocket.
# projectilestyle Optional field after projectiletype: cell 0-15 in the 4x4
#                rocketprojectile.png atlas, read left-to-right then top-to-bottom.
# explosionstyle Optional field after projectilestyle: 0=explosionsprites.png,
#                1=explosionsprites1.png, 2=explosionsprites2.png, and so on.
# explosionframetime Milliseconds per 32x32 frame; 16 frames play row-major.
# name           Internal name, maximum 14 characters and no spaces.
#                Normal guns load sfx/NAME.wav and sfx/NAMEreload.wav.
#                Missing files fall back to AK47 sounds for primary weapons,
#                GLOCK sounds for secondary weapons, KNIFE sounds for knives,
#                and the pin-pull sound for grenades.
#

# CODE AND ASSET CHECKLIST
# BuyMenu.cpp          No edit needed; category and teams register it.
# GameStateLoading.cpp No change for normal sounds. Edit only to reuse another
#                      gun's sounds or to add special equipment sound handling.
# Person.cpp           Edit only for a new grenade type. Pellets and scoped
#                      recoil are controlled by this file.
# Game.cpp             No edit needed for scopes; scope controls the camera.
# GameStatePlay.cpp    No edit needed for scopes; scope controls bot cameras.
# AI.cpp               Optional: change bot purchase selection to include it.
# guns.PNG             Add the hand sprite in the cell matching the new ID.
# gunsground.png       Add the ground sprite in the same matching ID cell.
# sfx/NAME.wav         Fire sound required for a normal weapon.
# sfx/NAMEreload.wav   Reload sound required for a normal weapon.
#
# Fire mode is already data-driven for every weapon type. Do not edit code just
# to choose SEMI or AUTO; set the firemode field above to 0 or 1.
#
# EXAMPLE: semi-automatic pistol for both teams using muzzle flash 2 at ID 64
# 64 20 120 0.25 15 5 1900 1.15 1.0 0.0 700 1 0 1 0 1 3 2 NEWPISTOL
# Increase the first-line count and provide both sprites. Sounds are optional.
